 {"id": "INT-CI-036", "title": "CI red on main at f327db24: test-counts.json drift (252 suites/2094 tests recorded vs 253/2098 live) — run 41865466392", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-04T17:27:42Z", "reasoning": "The test job fails at step 'Assert test-counts.json matches live suite' with the literal line 'GAP-012 drift: test-counts.json (252 suites, 2094 tests) != live (253 suites, 2098 tests)'. This is the third recurrence of the same class (INT-CI-3, INT-CI-033, INT-CI-034 all closed on the same drift), so the durable fix matters more than the number bump.", "acceptance_criteria": "FIX: regenerate the counts with the repo's own writer (scripts/sync-agents-md-counts.sh against a fresh vitest run) so test-counts.json and any AGENTS.md count lines carry the true live numbers, committed together with the change that moved them. PASS: bash scripts/sync-agents-md-counts.sh --check <fresh vitest output> exits 0 at HEAD, and the next CI run on main is green on the test job. NOT acceptable: hand-editing the numbers to silence the gate without a live suite run behind them.", "updated_at": "2026-11-05T17:55:12Z", "detail": {"fingerprint": "7e3201003e3a33e011460eddef2fbc6ae81c958166bb3e0293718593c25eb633", "evidence": [{"run_id":"41865466392","ts":"2026-11-04T17:27:42Z"},{"run_id":"fc56e15e","ts":"2026-11-05T17:55:12Z"}]}, "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "already-satisfied on main: fresh suite 255/2124 matches test-counts.json (--check exit 0); counts bumps ride their suite commits; CI green at 57f58cf9, was red at f327db24 on that exact assert", "foreman_note": "claimed by harden-loop 2026-11-05T17:45:49Z; verify-only path: premise may already be satisfied — proof = fresh vitest run + sync-agents-md-counts.sh --check at origin/main (57f58cf9) + green CI on main\n\nVerified, not re-implemented (premise already satisfied on main at 57f58cf9, gitrei