 {"id": "HARDEN-DUCKBRAIN-005", "title": "[P1] A fresh clone of main cannot install: pnpm-lock.yaml has no importers[packages/sdk], so CI's pnpm install --frozen-lockfile aborts before any test runs", "priority": "P1", "status": "complete", "complexity": 1, "created_at": "2026-11-06T21:56:57Z", "created_by": null, "reasoning": "Reproduced 2026-11-06 from a --depth 1 clone of main at 1a4b2242 (file:// clone, 27M .git): 'pnpm install --frozen-lockfile' exits with ERR_PNPM_PACKAGE_MANAGER_NO_IMPORTER \u2014 'Cannot install with \"frozen-lockfile\" because pnpm-lock.yaml has no importers[\"packages/sdk\"] entry'. packages/sdk was added by SDK-PARITY-001 (1c3fbf67, 2026-11-06 11:40 -0500) and declares no dependencies, yet pnpm still requires an importer per workspace package (pnpm-workspace.yaml lists packages/*). 'pnpm install --no-frozen-lockfile' succeeds and does NOT rewrite the lockfile, so the tree looks clean while the frozen install CI runs is broken \u2014 the hardening loop's own STEP 3 (worktree + frozen install) fails on this and had to fall back to --no-frozen-lockfile. This is the 'stranger with a fresh clone' boundary failing at the very first command.", "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: on a fresh 'git clone --depth 1 <main>' into an empty store, 'pnpm install --frozen-lockfile' exits 0 with no ERR_PNPM_PACKAGE_MANAGER_NO_IMPORTER. PASS: pnpm-lock.yaml carries an importer entry for EVERY workspace package listed by pnpm-workspace.yaml ('.', 'packages/ui', 'packages/sdk'), regenerated by pnpm (--lockfile-only), never hand-edited. PASS: the same frozen install is shown green in a scratch clone at the landed commit (paste the transcript), and test-counts.json is untouched (no suite change). FALSIFIER: the pre-fix transcript above (clone at 1a4b2242 -> frozen install aborts before installing anything).", "updated_at": "2026-11-06T22:52:03Z", "detail": {"fingerprint": "a7dc4b0774c18d03069caed9692f19db1ed6e51510a10be681fb516b7d3160cd", "evidence": [{"run_id":"68a03820","ts":"2026-11-06T22:52:03Z"}]}, "foreman_note": "claimed by harden-loop 2026-11-06T22:45:35Z; worktree wt/HARDEN-DUCKBRAIN-005\n\nacd44985 (ff-merged to main; verified ancestor of origin/main and pnpm-lock.yaml:231 in that tree). AC-1 PROVEN: pre-fix clone at 9781fad1 -> pnpm install --frozen-lockfile EXIT=1 ERR_PNPM_PACKAGE_MANAGER_NO_IMPORTER; post-fix clone of origin/main at acd44985 with empty store -> \"Lockfile is up to date\" Done EXIT=0. AC-2 PROVEN: parsed importer keys = ['.','packages/sdk','packages/ui'] = every package from pnpm-workspace.yaml; lockfile diff is exactly \"packages/sdk: {}\" (2 lines), written by pnpm --lockfile-only, not hand-edited. MECHANISM NOTE (pnpm quirk, NOT fixed here): pnpm 12.4.2 will not re-add a MISSING empty importer on a plain --lockfile-only (prints Done, writes nothing, while frozen install still refuses; reproduced in a minimal workspace); the entry was produced by pnpm by temporarily declaring a dep in packages/sdk, running --lockfile-only, reverting the manifest, then re-running --lockfile-only so pnpm pruned the temp dep and kept the empty importer. Any future dep-free workspace package hits the same wall. AC-3 PROVEN: pnpm test:run 280 suites / 2385 tests passed (94.5s); test-counts.json untouched and equal to live totals. DID NOT PROVE: GitHub CI run for this commit (not dispatched).", "commit_hash": "acd44985", "ci_result": "SKIP"}
 {"id": "HARDEN-DUCKBRAIN-006", "title": "[P1] Legacy .table.json INSERT writes NO DB-SUPA-5 change record: the feed never replays those inserts, and a create-then-delete inside one commit window poisons the namespace feed with CHANGELOG_CORRUPT (permanently, for every subscriber)", "priority": "P1", "status": "complete", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-11-07T01:48:37Z", "created_by": null, "reasoning": "Reproduced 2026-11-07 from a fresh clone of origin/main c736278b + scratch daemon (port 28733, apikey auth, own DUCKBRAIN_NAMESPACES_PATH): POST {\"id\":3} then DELETE ?pk=eq.3 inside the 30s commit debounce on a LEGACY tables/widgets.table.json table => audit ledger carried the tombstone only (no insert record) => GET /api/ns/harden/changes answered 500 {\"code\":\"CHANGELOG_CORRUPT\",\"error\":\"change record at '_audit/current.jsonl:6' has no data row with the recorded content hash in committed target 'tables/widgets.jsonl'\"} and the daemon logged the same line at realtime warm-up. Mechanism: insertTableRows() serves .table.json tables through a bare file append (appendRowsToTable) with no change record, while updateTableRows/deleteTableRows call recordTableMutationAudit. REPLAY-BIRTH-DEATH-001's sameWindowBirthAndDeath() recognises the born-and-died case ONLY as a matched pair (same table+key+contentHash) in one commit diff, and a tombstone is deliberately excluded from the resolveDataRowByKey fallback, so with no birth record the tombstone resolves at neither ref and the whole namespace feed fails closed forever. Second consequence even without the delete: those inserts were silently absent from the change stream while updates/deletes of the same table were present. Scope note: schema.json tables were never affected (the serializer writes both records); the same-window insert+UPDATE+delete sequence is a separate, still-open limitation shared by both paths (filed as HARDEN-DUCKBRAIN-007).", "acceptance_criteria": "1) insertTableRows() writes ONE accepted DB-SUPA-5 change record per inserted row for legacy .table.json declarations, carrying targetPath, key, tombstone:false and contentHash == contentHashFor(the exact appended line); tables with no declared primary keep the record-less append shape (REST verbs cannot address them). 2) Falsifier: a new test src/http/realtime/legacy-insert-change-record.test.ts shows POST on a legacy table produces a birth record and the feed replays it, and POST+DELETE inside one commit window leaves a matched insert/tombstone pair whose commit derives WITHOUT CHANGELOG_CORRUPT (both cases FAIL on pre-fix src/tables/operations.ts: 0 records and 1 record respectively). 3) Live scratch-daemon proof: pre-fix build answers 500 CHANGELOG_CORRUPT for /api/ns/<ns>/changes after the same two calls; fixed build answers 200 with a ready frame carrying a head cursor. 4) pnpm test:run green with test-counts.json updated in the same commit.", "updated_at": "2026-11-07T01:50:44Z", "detail": {"fingerprint": "e3eac786a444629f860d0375f4588196d1937b1fc8ebbac6cade44c6ae3a809c", "evidence": [{"run_id":"hardenloop-2026-11-07T01-58Z-wt-HARDEN-DUCKBRAIN-006","ts":"2026-11-07T01:50:44Z"}]}, "foreman_note": "PROVEN (1) mechanism: src/tables/operations.ts insertTableRows() legacy branch now calls recordTableMutationAudit per inserted row with dataLine = serializeRowLine(declaration,row) (the same bytes appendRowsToTable wrote) and targetPath = the appended file; no-primary tables keep the record-less append (REST verbs cannot address them). (2) Falsifier: new src/http/realtime/legacy-insert-change-record.test.ts — 'an accepted insert appends a change record and replays as a change event' and 'an insert and its delete inside one commit window do not poison the feed'. Both FAIL on pre-fix code (git stash of operations.ts => 'expected [] to have a length of 1 but got +0' and 'expected [ { …(11) } ] to have a length of 2 but got 1') and PASS on the fix. (3) LIVE pre-fix repro (scratch daemon 28733, origin-main build 