-{"id": "HARDEN-DUCKBRAIN-007", "title": "[P2] Namespaces whose committed history already contains an orphan change record stay poisoned after HARDEN-DUCKBRAIN-006 — need a read-only census and an owner decision on repair vs replay tolerance", "priority": "P2", "status": "in_progress", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-07T01:48:42Z", "created_by": null, "reasoning": "HARDEN-DUCKBRAIN-006 stops NEW orphan records (legacy insert+delete inside one commit window), but it cannot heal a namespace whose git history already carries one: deriveCommitChanges walks the committed audit ledger, so a pre-fix tombstone with no birth record still throws CHANGELOG_CORRUPT for every subscriber of that namespace, and the daemon logs it at realtime warm-up (observed on the 2026-11-07 scratch namespace: 'change record at _audit/current.jsonl:6 has no data row with the recorded content hash'). Two other shapes share the class and are NOT fixed by 006: (a) insert + UPDATE + delete of the same row inside one commit window (hashes differ, so the pair rule cannot match — any path, schema.json included), (b) a legacy insert that was never recorded at all, which silently missing from the change stream for that commit. Repair options are owner-gated because they touch production git history: (i) append a synthetic birth record in a new commit (no history rewrite), (ii) widen replay tolerance for an unresolvable tombstone whose row is absent at child by key (weakens the fabricated-hash guard — needs an explicit ruling), (iii) leave as-is and document per-namespace. A read-only census is dispatchable: for each namespace under the namespaces root, derive commits from HEAD and count CHANGELOG_CORRUPT occurrences without mutating anything.", "acceptance_criteria": "1) A read-only census reports, per namespace, whether any commit in its committed audit ledger derives CHANGELOG_CORRUPT, with the offending record path/line and the date of the commit (paste the per-namespace counts for the full pr