+- id: RLS-001
+  title: 'RLS-001: declare row-level security per (namespace, table) in the schema.json
+    declaration, enforced on every data verb and the change feed'
+  criteria:
+  - A policy {read:{column,equals}, write:{column,equals}} is declared in the SAME
+    schema.json table definition (no second format); column must be a declared column
+    and equals is a literal or a .id/.name principal reference; malformed policy is
+    a declaration error, never silently no policy.
+  - 'Enforced AFTER the existing grant check on GET, PATCH, DELETE, PUT, insert, the
+    transaction envelope and the change feed: excluded rows are neither revealed nor
+    mutated, and the feed applies the same predicate on replay and live delivery.'
+  - A PATCH that matches only rows the policy excludes returns the SAME {updated:0}
+    shape as a PATCH that matched nothing (no existence oracle).
+  - A row missing the policy column is DENIED (never treated as everybody's row).
+  - Row-policy denials are audited in the namespace audit with reason 'row_policy',
+    distinct from the grant layer's 'table_grant'.
